## `do-next-available-task` and remote registration

- By default the CLI runs integration-branch sync (`git fetch`, checkout, `merge --ff-only`) and **pushes** the registration commit. The one exception is **`--local`**: it registers in this checkout without fetch, merge or push, so peers cannot see the claim until you push the integration branch. Use it only when asked (offline, private spike); there is no `--no-sync` or `--no-push-registry`.
- `specy-road abort-task-pickup` **pushes** the integration branch after removing the registry row (no `--no-push`).
- Prefer a **failed `git push`** with a clear error over giving up before the claim is on **`remote/<integration-branch>`**; fix auth/network and retry, or push manually per `docs/dev-workflow.md`.
